        "</style>\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "# Introduction & research questions\n",
        "\n",
        "This report replaces three earlier working documents\n",
        "(`notebooks/fire_history_eda.ipynb`, `notebooks/animal_sightings.ipynb`,\n",
        "`reports/fire_heat_recovery_analysis.qmd`, and\n",
        "`reports/australia_recovery_gap_analysis.qmd`) with a single,\n",
        "non-redundant pipeline: raw fire-history shapefiles in, a fully-tested\n",
        "answer out. Every dataset is built exactly once; every downstream\n",
        "section reuses that one copy rather than re-loading or re-deriving it.\n",
        "\n",
        "Two connected questions are asked, in order:\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Q1 (§4, no heat).** Among divisions that keep re-burning, does\n",
        "> vegetation (NDVI) or wildlife-sighting recovery show a progressively\n",
        "> **weaker** trend the more often a division has had a major fire?\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Q2 (§5-§11, the headline question).** Does **post-fire heat\n",
        "> exposure** widen the gap between vegetation recovery and wildlife\n",
        "> recovery -- i.e. does the reassuring \"it's green again\" signal from\n",
        "> satellite NDVI become a progressively worse proxy for \"the habitat is\n",
        "> fine\" as the years after a fire get hotter?\n",
        "\n",
        "Q1 is answered at **division level** using fire frequency alone (the\n",
        "original EDA notebook's question). Q2 reframes the same underlying data\n",
        "at **event level** (one row per major fire, not per division) and adds\n",
        "a fourth dataset -- daily heat exposure -- so recovery can be tested\n",
        "against *climate stress* specifically, not just how often a place burns.\n",
        "Q2's event-level design also gives far more statistical power than Q1's\n",
        "division-level aggregates.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Dataset | Role | Source |\n",
        "|----|----|----|\n",
        "| Fire history shapefiles, 7 states/territories | disturbance events: location, date, area | NSW (NPWS), QLD (QPWS), VIC (DEECA), SA, TAS, WA (DBCA), NT |\n",
        "| `FAO/GAUL/2015/level2` admin-2 boundaries | LGA-level division geometries | Google Earth Engine |\n",
        "| `AusENDVI-clim_MCD43A4...nc` | vegetation recovery signal (NDVI), 1982-2022 | Gap-filled MODIS NDVI climatology |\n",
        "| ERA5-Land daily max temperature | post-fire heat exposure, relative to each division's own baseline | Earth Engine, 1982-2022 |\n",
        "| Koala / greater glider / yellow-bellied glider / yellow-tailed black-cockatoo / powerful owl / little lorikeet occurrences | wildlife presence (6 canopy/hollow-dependent indicator species) | Atlas of Living Australia (`galah`), 1990-2026, all 7 states/territories |\n",
        "\n",
        "# Setup"
      ],
      "id": "7675ceb8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import os\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from scipy import stats\n",
        "import statsmodels.formula.api as smf\n",
        "from statsmodels.stats.outliers_influence import variance_inflation_factor\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import geopandas as gpd\n",
        "import plotly.express as px\n",
        "\n",
        "DATA_DIR = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \"..\", \"data\")  # report lives in reports/, data lives in ../data\n",
        "pd.set_option(\"display.width\", 140)\n",
        "\n",
        "def sig(p, thresh=0.05):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Small helper so every significance claim below is read live off the\n",
        "    current p-value rather than typed as a fixed claim in prose.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return f\"significant (p = {p:.3g} < {thresh})\" if p < thresh else f\"not significant (p = {p:.3g} ≥ {thresh})\""
      ],
      "id": "bed5c0d6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Data sources & processing pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "Each subsection documents how one cached file in `data/` was built. The\n",
        "raw-data steps (reading multi-gigabyte shapefiles/netCDF, calling Earth\n",
        "Engine, calling the ALA API) are shown as code but marked `eval: false`\n",
        "-- they need local raw data and/or authenticated cloud access that this\n",
        "report doesn't assume is present at render time -- immediately followed\n",
        "by a **live** cell that loads the resulting cached CSV and reports the\n",
        "real, current numbers. Every dataset below is loaded **exactly once**;\n",
        "every later section reuses that same in-memory copy.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Fire history: loading and standardising 7 jurisdictions\n",
        "\n",
        "Each state/territory publishes its fire-history layer with different\n",
        "column names and CRSes (NSW/QLD: GDA94 lat/lon, VIC: VicGrid94 projected\n",
        "metres, etc.) -- reproject everything to EPSG:4326 and pull out a common\n",
        "`(state, start_date, area_ha, geometry)` schema so they can be combined.\n",
        "The Northern Territory layer carries its own per-record `state`\n",
        "attribute (border-adjacent fires are sometimes attributed to\n",
        "neighbouring QLD/WA/SA), so that attribute is used directly rather than\n",
        "hardcoding \"Northern Territory\" for every row."
      ],
      "id": "23159e02"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "#| code-summary: \"Appendix: loading & standardising the 7 state/territory fire-history layers\"\n",
        "FIRE_SHAPEFILES = {\n",
        "    \"New South Wales\": os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"NSW_fire_history\", \"NPWSFireHistory.shp\"),\n",
        "    \"Queensland\": os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"QLD_fire_history\", \"Fire_history___QPWS.shp\"),\n",
        "    \"Victoria\": os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"VIC_fire_history\", \"gda94_victoriagrid\", \"esrishape\",\n",
        "                              \"whole_of_dataset\", \"victoria\", \"FIRE\", \"FIRE_HISTORY_LASTBURNT.shp\"),\n",
        "    \"South Australia\": os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"SA_fire_history\", \"FIREMGT_FireHistory_GDA2020.shp\"),\n",
        "    \"Tasmania\": os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"TAS_fire_history\", \"list_fire_history_statewide.gdb\"),\n",
        "    \"Western Australia\": os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"WA_fire_history\", \"DBCA_Fire_History_DBCA_060.shp\"),\n",
        "    \"Northern Territory\": os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"NA_fire_history\", \"NT_FireHistory_SHP.shp\"),\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "def _naive_dates(series):\n",
        "    # Concatenating tz-aware dates (e.g. TAS's File Geodatabase) with tz-naive\n",
        "    # ones forces the combined column to dtype=object, breaking groupby min/max.\n",
        "    parsed = pd.to_datetime(series, errors=\"coerce\")\n",
        "    if getattr(parsed.dt, \"tz\", None) is not None:\n",
        "        parsed = parsed.dt.tz_localize(None)\n",
        "    return parsed\n",
        "\n",
        "def load_nsw(path):\n",
        "    gdf = gpd.read_file(path).to_crs(4326)\n",
        "    return gpd.GeoDataFrame({\"state\": \"New South Wales\", \"start_date\": _naive_dates(gdf[\"StartDate\"]),\n",
        "                              \"area_ha\": gdf[\"AreaHa\"], \"geometry\": gdf.geometry}, crs=4326)\n",
        "\n",
        "def load_qld(path):\n",
        "    gdf = gpd.read_file(path).to_crs(4326)\n",
        "    return gpd.GeoDataFrame({\"state\": \"Queensland\", \"start_date\": _naive_dates(gdf[\"ignitionda\"]),\n",
        "                              \"area_ha\": gdf[\"area_ha\"], \"geometry\": gdf.geometry}, crs=4326)\n",
        "\n",
        "def load_vic(path):\n",
        "    gdf = gpd.read_file(path).to_crs(4326)\n",
        "    return gpd.GeoDataFrame({\"state\": \"Victoria\", \"start_date\": _naive_dates(gdf[\"START_DATE\"]),\n",
        "                              \"area_ha\": gdf[\"AREA_HA\"], \"geometry\": gdf.geometry}, crs=4326)\n",
        "\n",
        "def load_sa(path):\n",
        "    gdf = gpd.read_file(path).to_crs(4326)\n",
        "    return gpd.GeoDataFrame({\"state\": \"South Australia\", \"start_date\": _naive_dates(gdf[\"FIREDATE\"]),\n",
        "                              \"area_ha\": gdf[\"HECTARES\"], \"geometry\": gdf.geometry}, crs=4326)\n",
        "\n",
        "def load_tas(path):\n",
        "    gdf = gpd.read_file(path, layer=\"list_fire_history_statewide\").to_crs(4326)  # File Geodatabase, needs the layer name\n",
        "    return gpd.GeoDataFrame({\"state\": \"Tasmania\", \"start_date\": _naive_dates(gdf[\"IGN_DATE\"]),\n",
        "                              \"area_ha\": gdf[\"FIRE_AR_HA\"], \"geometry\": gdf.geometry}, crs=4326)\n",
        "\n",
        "def load_wa(path):\n",
        "    gdf = gpd.read_file(path).to_crs(4326)\n",
        "    return gpd.GeoDataFrame({\"state\": \"Western Australia\", \"start_date\": _naive_dates(gdf[\"fih_date1\"]),\n",
        "                              \"area_ha\": gdf[\"fih_hectar\"], \"geometry\": gdf.geometry}, crs=4326)\n",
        "\n",
        "def load_nt(path):\n",
        "    # Border-adjacent records may carry a neighbouring state's own attribution --\n",
        "    # not deduplicated against the QLD/WA/SA loaders above; flagged in Limitations.\n",
        "    gdf = gpd.read_file(path).to_crs(4326)\n",
        "    state_map = {\"NT\": \"Northern Territory\", \"Qld\": \"Queensland\", \"QLD\": \"Queensland\",\n",
        "                 \"WA\": \"Western Australia\", \"SA\": \"South Australia\"}\n",
        "    return gpd.GeoDataFrame({\"state\": gdf[\"state\"].map(lambda s: state_map.get(s, s)),\n",
        "                              \"start_date\": _naive_dates(gdf[\"ignition_d\"]),\n",
        "                              \"area_ha\": gdf[\"area_ha\"], \"geometry\": gdf.geometry}, crs=4326)\n",
        "\n",
        "fires = pd.concat([\n",
        "    load_nsw(FIRE_SHAPEFILES[\"New South Wales\"]), load_qld(FIRE_SHAPEFILES[\"Queensland\"]),\n",
        "    load_vic(FIRE_SHAPEFILES[\"Victoria\"]), load_sa(FIRE_SHAPEFILES[\"South Australia\"]),\n",
        "    load_tas(FIRE_SHAPEFILES[\"Tasmania\"]), load_wa(FIRE_SHAPEFILES[\"Western Australia\"]),\n",
        "    load_nt(FIRE_SHAPEFILES[\"Northern Territory\"]),\n",
        "], ignore_index=True)\n",
        "fires = gpd.GeoDataFrame(fires, geometry=\"geometry\", crs=4326)\n",
        "fires = fires[fires.geometry.notna() & fires.geometry.is_valid]\n",
        "print(f\"Total fire records: {len(fires)}\")"
      ],
      "id": "601a24dd",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Admin-2 (LGA-level) division boundaries\n",
        "\n",
        "A small one-time vector pull from Earth Engine (`FAO/GAUL/2015/level2`),\n",
        "cached locally so it only hits Earth Engine once."
      ],
      "id": "03af0143"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "#| code-summary: \"Appendix: pulling admin-2 division boundaries from Earth Engine\"\n",
        "import ee\n",
        "import geemap\n",
        "\n",
        "ADMIN2_CACHE = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"au_admin2_boundaries.geojson\")\n",
        "REQUIRED_STATES = [\"New South Wales\", \"Victoria\", \"Queensland\", \"South Australia\",\n",
        "                   \"Tasmania\", \"Western Australia\", \"Northern Territory\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "ee.Initialize(project=\"project-868d3a54-1ed8-47ec-9ad\")\n",
        "gaul = ee.FeatureCollection(\"FAO/GAUL/2015/level2\")\n",
        "au_fc = (gaul.filter(ee.Filter.eq(\"ADM0_NAME\", \"Australia\"))\n",
        "              .filter(ee.Filter.inList(\"ADM1_NAME\", REQUIRED_STATES)))\n",
        "admin2 = geemap.ee_to_gdf(au_fc).set_crs(4326, allow_override=True)\n",
        "admin2.to_file(ADMIN2_CACHE, driver=\"GeoJSON\")"
      ],
      "id": "984f6308",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "admin2 = gpd.read_file(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"au_admin2_boundaries.geojson\"))[[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\", \"geometry\"]]\n",
        "print(f\"{len(admin2)} admin-2 divisions loaded, covering: {sorted(admin2['ADM1_NAME'].unique())}\")"
      ],
      "id": "dc64309a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Defining \"fire-prone\" divisions\n",
        "\n",
        "Fires are spatially joined to divisions on the fire polygon's\n",
        "**centroid** (fast point-in-polygon; fine here since only \"which\n",
        "division is this fire mostly in\" is needed, not exact boundary\n",
        "overlap -- this keeps the 440k-row Victorian layer fast to join).\n",
        "Fire count alone favours Victoria, which has ~440k small recorded burns\n",
        "(median ~11 ha) spread over few divisions, versus NSW/QLD's far fewer\n",
        "but much larger fires. Requiring **both** a minimum fire count *and* a\n",
        "minimum average area per fire targets divisions with frequent,\n",
        "*significant* fire activity, not just lots of small planned burns."
      ],
      "id": "2f103c00"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "#| code-summary: \"Appendix: spatial join + fire-prone division threshold -> fire_prone_divisions.csv\"\n",
        "import warnings\n",
        "\n",
        "fire_points = fires.copy()\n",
        "with warnings.catch_warnings():\n",
        "    warnings.simplefilter(\"ignore\", category=UserWarning)\n",
        "    fire_points[\"geometry\"] = fires.geometry.centroid  # only need \"roughly which division\", not a precise centroid\n",
        "\n",
        "joined = gpd.sjoin(fire_points, admin2, how=\"left\", predicate=\"within\")\n",
        "\n",
        "division_summary = (\n",
        "    joined.dropna(subset=[\"ADM2_NAME\"])\n",
        "    .groupby([\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"])\n",
        "    .agg(fire_count=(\"area_ha\", \"size\"), total_area_ha=(\"area_ha\", \"sum\"),\n",
        "         earliest_fire=(\"start_date\", \"min\"), latest_fire=(\"start_date\", \"max\"))\n",
        "    .reset_index()\n",
        ")\n",
        "division_summary[\"avg_area_ha_per_fire\"] = division_summary[\"total_area_ha\"] / division_summary[\"fire_count\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "MIN_FIRE_COUNT = 178     # median fire_count across all divisions with >=1 fire\n",
        "MIN_AVG_AREA_HA = 184    # median avg_area_ha_per_fire across the same set\n",
        "filtered = division_summary[\n",
        "    (division_summary[\"fire_count\"] >= MIN_FIRE_COUNT) &\n",
        "    (division_summary[\"avg_area_ha_per_fire\"] >= MIN_AVG_AREA_HA)\n",
        "].sort_values(\"fire_count\", ascending=False)\n",
        "filtered.to_csv(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"fire_prone_divisions.csv\"), index=False)"
      ],
      "id": "fdb80c69",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "fire_prone = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"fire_prone_divisions.csv\"))\n",
        "print(f\"{len(fire_prone)} fire-prone divisions, by state:\")\n",
        "print(fire_prone.groupby(\"ADM1_NAME\").size().sort_values(ascending=False))"
      ],
      "id": "8597b6e7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Requiring both a high fire count *and* large average fire size currently\n",
        "skews the list toward NSW/QLD/WA -- Victoria's fires are individually\n",
        "small (median ~11 ha), so it drops out entirely at these thresholds;\n",
        "lowering `MIN_AVG_AREA_HA` would bring it back in.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Major fire events\n",
        "\n",
        "The raw layers mix routine hazard-reduction burns with genuine\n",
        "wildfires, and at LGA scale almost every fire-prone division has at\n",
        "least one fire recorded in almost every year -- so a naive fire count\n",
        "gives virtually no fire-free baseline to compare against. Fires\n",
        "`>= 10,000 ha` are treated as a \"major\" (landscape-scale) fire,\n",
        "separating real wildfires from routine hazard-reduction blocks."
      ],
      "id": "72e8b3e0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "#| code-summary: \"Appendix: aggregating to major fire events -> fire_events_by_division_year.csv\"\n",
        "MAJOR_FIRE_HA = 10000  # landscape-scale burn threshold\n",
        "\n",
        "fire_events = (\n",
        "    joined.dropna(subset=[\"ADM2_NAME\", \"start_date\"])\n",
        "    .merge(filtered[[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"]], on=[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"], how=\"inner\")\n",
        "    .assign(year=lambda d: d[\"start_date\"].dt.year, is_major=lambda d: d[\"area_ha\"] >= MAJOR_FIRE_HA)\n",
        "    .groupby([\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\", \"year\"])\n",
        "    .agg(fire_events=(\"area_ha\", \"size\"), total_area_ha=(\"area_ha\", \"sum\"),\n",
        "         max_area_ha=(\"area_ha\", \"max\"), major_fires=(\"is_major\", \"sum\"))\n",
        "    .reset_index()\n",
        ")\n",
        "fire_events[\"year\"] = fire_events[\"year\"].astype(int)\n",
        "fire_events.to_csv(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"fire_events_by_division_year.csv\"), index=False)"
      ],
      "id": "60c20277",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "fire_events = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"fire_events_by_division_year.csv\"))\n",
        "major = fire_events[fire_events.major_fires > 0].copy()\n",
        "print(f\"{len(fire_events)} division-year rows; {len(major)} contain at least one fire >= 10,000 ha, \"\n",
        "      f\"across states: {sorted(major['ADM1_NAME'].unique())}\")"
      ],
      "id": "52945c97",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Vegetation recovery: annual NDVI per division\n",
        "\n",
        "Each division polygon is rasterised against the NDVI grid with\n",
        "`regionmask` (one boolean mask per division), then averaged over each\n",
        "division's pixels for every year, 1982-2022 -- giving one NDVI time\n",
        "series per division rather than per pixel."
      ],
      "id": "a8afa0e9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "#| code-summary: \"Appendix: NDVI extraction from the AusENDVI netCDF -> ndvi_annual_by_division.csv\"\n",
        "import xarray as xr\n",
        "import regionmask\n",
        "\n",
        "NDVI_NC = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"AusENDVI-clim_MCD43A4_gapfilled_1982_2022_0.1.0.nc\")\n",
        "NDVI_VAR = \"AusENDVI_clim_MCD43A4\"\n",
        "\n",
        "admin2_fire_prone = admin2.merge(filtered[[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"]], on=[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"], how=\"inner\")\n",
        "\n",
        "ds = xr.open_dataset(NDVI_NC, engine=\"netcdf4\")\n",
        "annual = ds[NDVI_VAR].groupby(\"time.year\").mean(dim=\"time\").load()\n",
        "mask3D = regionmask.mask_3D_geopandas(admin2_fire_prone, annual.longitude, annual.latitude)\n",
        "div_annual = annual.where(mask3D).mean(dim=[\"latitude\", \"longitude\"], skipna=True).compute()\n",
        "\n",
        "region_states = admin2_fire_prone.loc[mask3D.region.values, \"ADM1_NAME\"].values\n",
        "region_names = admin2_fire_prone.loc[mask3D.region.values, \"ADM2_NAME\"].values\n",
        "ndvi_by_division = div_annual.to_pandas()\n",
        "ndvi_by_division.columns = pd.MultiIndex.from_arrays([region_states, region_names], names=[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"])\n",
        "ndvi_by_division = ndvi_by_division.T\n",
        "ndvi_by_division.to_csv(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"ndvi_annual_by_division.csv\"))"
      ],
      "id": "80642a9c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "ndvi = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"ndvi_annual_by_division.csv\")).set_index([\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"])\n",
        "ndvi.columns = ndvi.columns.astype(int)\n",
        "print(f\"NDVI table: {ndvi.shape[0]} divisions x {ndvi.shape[1]} years ({ndvi.columns.min()}-{ndvi.columns.max()})\")"
      ],
      "id": "74424295",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Post-fire heat exposure\n",
        "\n",
        "An ACORN-SAT (BOM station) bundle was considered first, but the network\n",
        "is only ~112 stations nation-wide with no bundled coordinates, which\n",
        "would add real spatial-matching error at LGA scale. Instead this pulls a\n",
        "**gridded** product -- ERA5-Land daily aggregates (`temperature_2m_max`,\n",
        "~11 km grid, same resolution class as the NDVI product) -- and averages\n",
        "it over each fire-prone division for every year, 1982-2022. Division\n",
        "geometries are simplified (`simplify(0.01 deg)`) before upload -- this\n",
        "cuts the Earth Engine request payload from ~12 MB to ~0.2 MB (avoiding a\n",
        "\"payload exceeds limit\" error), with no meaningful effect on a\n",
        "coarse-grid climate average."
      ],
      "id": "c0340e92"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "#| code-summary: \"Appendix: ERA5-Land heat exposure pull -> heat_stress_by_division_year.csv\"\n",
        "import ee\n",
        "import geemap\n",
        "\n",
        "ee.Initialize(project=\"project-868d3a54-1ed8-47ec-9ad\")\n",
        "admin2_fp = admin2.merge(fire_prone[[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"]], on=[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "admin2_fp[\"geometry\"] = admin2_fp.geometry.simplify(0.01, preserve_topology=True)\n",
        "fc_all = geemap.geopandas_to_ee(admin2_fp)\n",
        "\n",
        "era5 = ee.ImageCollection(\"ECMWF/ERA5_LAND/DAILY_AGGR\").select(\"temperature_2m_max\")\n",
        "HOT35_K, HOT40_K = 308.15, 313.15  # 35C / 40C in Kelvin\n",
        "\n",
        "def per_year(y):\n",
        "    y = ee.Number(y)\n",
        "    start = ee.Date.fromYMD(y, 1, 1)\n",
        "    coll = era5.filterDate(start, start.advance(1, \"year\"))\n",
        "    hot35 = coll.map(lambda img: img.gt(HOT35_K)).sum().rename(\"hot_days_ge35\")\n",
        "    hot40 = coll.map(lambda img: img.gt(HOT40_K)).sum().rename(\"hot_days_ge40\")\n",
        "    mean_tmax = coll.mean().subtract(273.15).rename(\"mean_tmax_c\")\n",
        "    combo = hot35.addBands(hot40).addBands(mean_tmax)\n",
        "    return combo.reduceRegions(collection=fc_all, reducer=ee.Reducer.mean(), scale=11132).map(lambda f: f.set(\"year\", y))\n",
        "\n",
        "all_rows = []\n",
        "for start_yr in range(1982, 2023, 5):  # chunked into 5-year requests to stay under payload/time limits\n",
        "    yrs = list(range(start_yr, min(start_yr + 5, 2023)))\n",
        "    yearly_fc = ee.FeatureCollection(ee.List(yrs).map(per_year)).flatten()\n",
        "    all_rows.extend([f[\"properties\"] for f in yearly_fc.getInfo()[\"features\"]])\n",
        "\n",
        "heat = pd.DataFrame(all_rows)\n",
        "heat[\"year\"] = heat[\"year\"].astype(int)\n",
        "heat = heat[[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\", \"year\", \"hot_days_ge35\", \"hot_days_ge40\", \"mean_tmax_c\"]]\n",
        "heat.to_csv(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"heat_stress_by_division_year.csv\"), index=False)"
      ],
      "id": "dbde90f0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "heat = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"heat_stress_by_division_year.csv\"))\n",
        "heat_piv = heat.pivot_table(index=[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"], columns=\"year\", values=\"hot_days_ge35\")\n",
        "heat_baseline_mean = heat_piv.mean(axis=1)\n",
        "print(f\"{heat.shape[0]} division-year rows, {heat['ADM2_NAME'].nunique()} divisions, \"\n",
        "      f\"{heat['year'].min()}-{heat['year'].max()}, states: {sorted(heat['ADM1_NAME'].unique())}\")"
      ],
      "id": "4fa03587",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Indicator-species sightings\n",
        "\n",
        "Six canopy/hollow-dependent species -- koala, greater glider,\n",
        "yellow-bellied glider, yellow-tailed black-cockatoo, powerful owl, and\n",
        "little lorikeet -- are pulled from the Atlas of Living Australia via\n",
        "`galah`, across all 7 states/territories, 1990-2026 (expanded from an\n",
        "earlier 3-species/3-state pull). Citizen-science reporting effort has\n",
        "grown enormously nation-wide since the 1990s (more observers, apps like\n",
        "iNaturalist), so each division's sightings are later expressed as a\n",
        "**share of that year's total sightings across all fire-prone\n",
        "divisions** -- a division whose wildlife is genuinely declining\n",
        "relative to everywhere else should lose share over time even while the\n",
        "nationwide raw count keeps climbing."
      ],
      "id": "58d4f505"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "#| code-summary: \"Appendix: pulling ALA occurrence records for the 6 indicator species (all states)\"\n",
        "import galah\n",
        "\n",
        "galah.galah_config(email=\"hieudonguyenthanh2906@gmail.com\")  # must be registered at ala.org.au first\n",
        "states_to_pull = [\"New South Wales\", \"Victoria\", \"Queensland\", \"South Australia\",\n",
        "                  \"Tasmania\", \"Western Australia\", \"Northern Territory\"]\n",
        "indicator_species = [\n",
        "    \"Phascolarctos cinereus\",  # Koala\n",
        "    \"Petauroides volans\",      # Greater Glider\n",
        "    \"Petaurus australis\",      # Yellow-bellied Glider\n",
        "    \"Zanda funerea\",           # Yellow-tailed Black-Cockatoo\n",
        "    \"Ninox strenua\",           # Powerful Owl\n",
        "    \"Parvipsitta pusilla\",     # Little Lorikeet\n",
        "]\n",
        "all_sightings = [\n",
        "    galah.atlas_occurrences(taxa=indicator_species,\n",
        "                             filters=[\"year>=1990\", \"year<=2026\", f\"stateProvince={state}\"])\n",
        "    for state in states_to_pull\n",
        "]\n",
        "pd.concat(all_sightings, ignore_index=True).to_csv(\n",
        "    os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"canopy_indicators_all_states.csv\"), index=False\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "ebabcdfa",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "#| code-summary: \"Appendix: spatial join of sightings onto fire-prone divisions -> animal_sightings_by_division_year.csv\"\n",
        "animals = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"canopy_indicators_all_states.csv\"),\n",
        "                       usecols=[\"decimalLatitude\", \"decimalLongitude\", \"eventDate\", \"scientificName\"])\n",
        "animals = animals.dropna(subset=[\"decimalLatitude\", \"decimalLongitude\", \"eventDate\"])\n",
        "animals[\"eventDate\"] = pd.to_datetime(animals[\"eventDate\"], errors=\"coerce\", utc=True)\n",
        "animals = animals.dropna(subset=[\"eventDate\"])\n",
        "animals[\"year\"] = animals[\"eventDate\"].dt.year\n",
        "\n",
        "animals_gdf = gpd.GeoDataFrame(animals, geometry=gpd.points_from_xy(animals[\"decimalLongitude\"], animals[\"decimalLatitude\"]), crs=4326)\n",
        "animals_joined = gpd.sjoin(animals_gdf, admin2, how=\"left\", predicate=\"within\")\n",
        "animals_joined = animals_joined.merge(fire_prone[[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"]], on=[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"], how=\"inner\")\n",
        "\n",
        "sightings_by_year = animals_joined.groupby([\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\", \"year\"]).size().rename(\"sightings\").reset_index()\n",
        "sightings_by_year.to_csv(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"animal_sightings_by_division_year.csv\"), index=False)"
      ],
      "id": "bf473342",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "sightings_raw = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"animal_sightings_by_division_year.csv\"))\n",
        "print(f\"{sightings_raw['sightings'].sum()} sightings across {sightings_raw['ADM2_NAME'].nunique()} divisions, \"\n",
        "      f\"states: {sorted(sightings_raw['ADM1_NAME'].unique())}\")"
      ],
      "id": "fe986720",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Q1 -- does fire frequency alone predict weaker recovery? {#sec-q1}\n",
        "\n",
        "Before bringing heat into the picture: among the fire-prone divisions\n",
        "above, do the ones that keep re-burning show a progressively **weaker**\n",
        "NDVI or wildlife-sighting recovery, or a long-term downward trend that\n",
        "tracks fire frequency alone? This section works at **division level**\n",
        "across the full 1982-2022 (NDVI) / 1995-2025 (sightings) record, using\n",
        "only `major` fire counts -- no heat data yet.\n",
        "\n",
        "The sightings-share pivot built here (`div_year`, `share_piv`,\n",
        "`total_sightings_per_div`) is reused as-is in §5 -- it is not\n",
        "recomputed."
      ],
      "id": "cd7ae794"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "div_year = sightings_raw.groupby([\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\", \"year\"])[\"sightings\"].sum().reset_index()\n",
        "total_per_year = div_year.groupby(\"year\")[\"sightings\"].sum().rename(\"total_sightings_all_divs\")\n",
        "div_year = div_year.merge(total_per_year, on=\"year\")\n",
        "div_year[\"share\"] = div_year[\"sightings\"] / div_year[\"total_sightings_all_divs\"]\n",
        "share_piv = div_year.pivot_table(index=[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"], columns=\"year\", values=\"share\")\n",
        "total_sightings_per_div = sightings_raw.groupby([\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"])[\"sightings\"].sum()"
      ],
      "id": "2fadb01b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## NDVI trend vs. major-fire frequency"
      ],
      "id": "3aa057e1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "NDVI_YEARS = ndvi.columns.values.astype(float)\n",
        "\n",
        "def linear_trend(row):\n",
        "    slope, _ = np.polyfit(NDVI_YEARS, row.values.astype(float), 1)\n",
        "    return slope\n",
        "\n",
        "ndvi_trend = ndvi.apply(linear_trend, axis=1).rename(\"ndvi_trend_per_yr\").reset_index()\n",
        "n_major = (major[major[\"year\"].between(1982, 2022)].groupby([\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"])[\"year\"].nunique()\n",
        "           .rename(\"n_major_fire_years\").reset_index())\n",
        "ndvi_trend = ndvi_trend.merge(n_major, on=[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"], how=\"left\")\n",
        "ndvi_trend[\"n_major_fire_years\"] = ndvi_trend[\"n_major_fire_years\"].fillna(0)\n",
        "ndvi_trend[\"major_fires_per_decade\"] = ndvi_trend[\"n_major_fire_years\"] / 41 * 10\n",
        "\n",
        "corr_ndvi = ndvi_trend[[\"major_fires_per_decade\", \"ndvi_trend_per_yr\"]].corr().iloc[0, 1]\n",
        "print(f\"Correlation(major_fires_per_decade, NDVI trend/yr) across {len(ndvi_trend)} fire-prone divisions: {corr_ndvi:.3f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 5))\n",
        "ax.scatter(ndvi_trend[\"major_fires_per_decade\"], ndvi_trend[\"ndvi_trend_per_yr\"], alpha=0.6)\n",
        "ax.axhline(0, color=\"grey\", lw=0.8)\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"major fires (>= 10,000 ha) per decade, 1982-2022\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"NDVI linear trend per year\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Repeated major fires vs long-term NDVI trend\\n(fire-prone LGA divisions)\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "1035e7d5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Sightings-share trend vs. major-fire frequency"
      ],
      "id": "513bdeda"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "YEAR_MIN, YEAR_MAX = 1995, 2025  # sightings are too sparse before ~1995 to trust a yearly share\n",
        "rows = []\n",
        "for (state, div), g in div_year.groupby([\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"]):\n",
        "    g = g[g[\"year\"].between(YEAR_MIN, YEAR_MAX)].sort_values(\"year\")\n",
        "    if len(g) < 8:\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "    slope, _ = np.polyfit(g[\"year\"].values.astype(float), g[\"share\"].values.astype(float), 1)\n",
        "    rel_slope = slope / g[\"share\"].mean() if g[\"share\"].mean() > 0 else np.nan\n",
        "    my = major[(major.ADM1_NAME == state) & (major.ADM2_NAME == div) & (major.year.between(YEAR_MIN, YEAR_MAX))]\n",
        "    rows.append({\"ADM1_NAME\": state, \"ADM2_NAME\": div, \"share_trend_rel_per_yr\": rel_slope,\n",
        "                 \"major_fires_per_decade\": my[\"year\"].nunique() / (YEAR_MAX - YEAR_MIN + 1) * 10})\n",
        "sightings_trend = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "\n",
        "corr_sight = sightings_trend[[\"major_fires_per_decade\", \"share_trend_rel_per_yr\"]].corr().iloc[0, 1]\n",
        "print(f\"Correlation(major_fires_per_decade, sightings-share trend) across {len(sightings_trend)} divisions: {corr_sight:.3f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 5))\n",
        "ax.scatter(sightings_trend[\"major_fires_per_decade\"], sightings_trend[\"share_trend_rel_per_yr\"], alpha=0.6, color=\"darkorange\")\n",
        "ax.axhline(0, color=\"grey\", lw=0.8)\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"major fires (>= 10,000 ha) per decade, 1995-2025\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"relative trend in share of all indicator-species sightings\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Repeated major fires vs sightings-share trend\\n(6 canopy/hollow-dependent indicator species)\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "8c0e18bb",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Case studies\n",
        "\n",
        "The fire-prone divisions with the largest single recorded fire *and*\n",
        "enough sighting data to be informative (>= 1,000 total sightings),\n",
        "NDVI and sightings-share plotted side by side with major-fire years\n",
        "marked."
      ],
      "id": "1484d103"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "case_study_candidates = (\n",
        "    major.groupby([\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"])\n",
        "    .agg(max_single_fire_ha=(\"max_area_ha\", \"max\"))\n",
        "    .reset_index()\n",
        "    .merge(div_year.groupby([\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"])[\"sightings\"].sum().rename(\"total_sightings\").reset_index(),\n",
        "           on=[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"])\n",
        ")\n",
        "case_study_divs = list(\n",
        "    case_study_candidates[case_study_candidates[\"total_sightings\"] >= 1000]\n",
        "    .sort_values(\"max_single_fire_ha\", ascending=False)\n",
        "    .head(4)[[\"ADM1_NAME\", \"ADM2_NAME\"]]\n",
        "    .itertuples(index=False, name=None)\n",
        ")\n",
        "print(\"Case-study divisions (largest single recorded fire, with enough sighting data to be informative):\")\n",
        "for state, div in case_study_divs:\n",
        "    print(\" -\", div, f\"({state})\")\n",
        "\n",
        "div_year_share_pct = div_year.copy()\n",
        "div_year_share_pct[\"share_pct\"] = 100 * div_year_share_pct[\"share\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(max(len(case_study_divs), 1), 2, figsize=(13, 3 * max(len(case_study_divs), 1)))\n",
        "if len(case_study_divs) == 1:\n",
        "    axes = axes.reshape(1, -1)\n",
        "for i, (state, div) in enumerate(case_study_divs):\n",
        "    ndvi_row = ndvi.loc[(state, div)]\n",
        "    fy = sorted(major[(major.ADM1_NAME == state) & (major.ADM2_NAME == div)][\"year\"].unique())\n",
        "\n",
        "    ax = axes[i, 0]\n",
        "    ax.plot(ndvi_row.index, ndvi_row.values, marker=\"o\", ms=3, color=\"seagreen\")\n",
        "    for y in fy:\n",
        "        if y in ndvi_row.index:\n",
        "            ax.axvline(y, color=\"firebrick\", alpha=0.15, lw=2)\n",
        "    ax.set_title(f\"{div} -- annual NDVI (red = major fire year)\")\n",
        "    ax.set_xlim(1982, 2022)\n",
        "\n",
        "    ax2 = axes[i, 1]\n",
        "    g = div_year_share_pct[(div_year_share_pct.ADM1_NAME == state) & (div_year_share_pct.ADM2_NAME == div)]\n",
        "    g = g.set_index(\"year\")[\"share_pct\"].reindex(range(YEAR_MIN, YEAR_MAX + 1), fill_value=0)\n",
        "    ax2.bar(g.index, g.values, color=\"steelblue\")\n",
        "    for y in fy:\n",
        "        if YEAR_MIN <= y <= YEAR_MAX:\n",
        "            ax2.axvline(y, color=\"firebrick\", alpha=0.15, lw=2)\n",
        "    ax2.set_title(f\"{div} -- share of all fire-prone-division sightings (%)\")\n",
        "    ax2.set_xlim(YEAR_MIN, YEAR_MAX)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "e64d6d7c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Q1 summary\n",
        "\n",
        "Correlation across fire-prone divisions is `{python} f\"{corr_ndvi:.2f}\"`\n",
        "for (major fires/decade, NDVI trend) and `{python} f\"{corr_sight:.2f}\"`\n",
        "for (major fires/decade, sightings-share trend). NDVI trend at this\n",
        "LGA-averaged, annual resolution shows little to no relationship with\n",
        "raw fire frequency -- vegetation greenness tends to rebound to, or\n",
        "above, its pre-fire level within a few years, repeatedly, regardless of\n",
        "how often a division has burnt. Wildlife-sightings share shows a\n",
        "clearer negative tendency: divisions burning more often lose a larger\n",
        "share of the regional sighting record over time, even after\n",
        "normalising for the nationwide rise in reporting effort. Read together\n",
        "this is consistent with a real ecological asymmetry rather than a data\n",
        "artefact -- leaf-level greenness recovers on a vegetation-growth\n",
        "timescale of a few years, while hollow-dependent species depend on\n",
        "habitat *structure* (large old trees with hollows) that takes decades\n",
        "to regenerate. Both correlations are division-level, EDA-strength\n",
        "signals (not controlled for heat, remoteness, or drought) -- §5-§11 now\n",
        "add heat exposure and move to event-level testing to put this asymmetry\n",
        "under a proper statistical test.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Building the event-level recovery dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "The analysis unit changes here from *division* to **individual major\n",
        "fire event** (one row per division x fire-year with a fire\n",
        "`>= 10,000 ha`) -- this gives far more statistical power than §4's\n",
        "division-level aggregates, and lets each event's own post-fire heat\n",
        "exposure be measured directly.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Recovery ratio (RRI)**, adapted from Frazier et al. (2018, *Remote\n",
        "Sensing of Environment* 205:32-45): `RRI = ARI / disturbance magnitude`,\n",
        "where disturbance magnitude is the pre-fire NDVI baseline (mean of the\n",
        "2 years before the fire) minus the fire-year NDVI value, and ARI is the\n",
        "best post-fire NDVI value (across `fire_year+3`, `+4`, `+5`, whichever\n",
        "are available) minus that same fire-year value. The paper uses a fixed\n",
        "`Y+4`/`Y+5` window on precisely-dated per-pixel LandTrendr breakpoints;\n",
        "here \"fire year\" is just the annual division-wide composite for that\n",
        "calendar year (a noisier proxy for the true disturbance trough), and the\n",
        "window is the best *available* of `+3`/`+4`/`+5` rather than fixed\n",
        "`+4`/`+5`, because NDVI data ends in 2022 and a fixed window would drop\n",
        "every fire from 2019 onward -- including Black Summer. Only defined\n",
        "when the disturbance magnitude is positive. The identical construction\n",
        "is applied to sightings share, with a small constant (`1e-6`) added\n",
        "throughout to avoid divide-by-zero, and is only computed for divisions\n",
        "with a real koala/glider/etc. presence (>= 200 total sightings) to avoid\n",
        "diluting the test with non-habitat divisions.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Post-fire heat exposure** = mean `hot_days_ge35`/yr over `fire_year`\n",
        "to `fire_year + 3`. **Heat anomaly** = that value minus the *same\n",
        "division's* long-run mean hot-day count -- isolating \"was this recovery\n",
        "window unusually hot for this place\", not just re-detecting that e.g.\n",
        "inland Queensland is hotter than alpine NSW."
      ],
      "id": "a777c463"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "PRE_YEARS, HEAT_POST_LAG, RECOVERY_POST_LAGS, SMOOTH = 2, 3, [3, 4, 5], 1e-6\n",
        "\n",
        "records = []\n",
        "for _, r in major.iterrows():\n",
        "    state, div, year = r[\"ADM1_NAME\"], r[\"ADM2_NAME\"], int(r[\"year\"])\n",
        "    key = (state, div)\n",
        "    if key not in ndvi.index or key not in heat_piv.index:\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "\n",
        "    ndvi_row, heat_row = ndvi.loc[key], heat_piv.loc[key]\n",
        "    pre_years = [year - k for k in range(1, PRE_YEARS + 1)]\n",
        "    heat_post_years = [year + k for k in range(0, HEAT_POST_LAG + 1)]\n",
        "    recovery_post_years = [year + k for k in RECOVERY_POST_LAGS]\n",
        "\n",
        "    pre_ndvi = [v for v in (ndvi_row.get(y) for y in pre_years) if pd.notna(v)]\n",
        "    y0_ndvi = ndvi_row.get(year)\n",
        "    post_ndvi = [v for v in (ndvi_row.get(y) for y in recovery_post_years) if pd.notna(v)]\n",
        "    if not pre_ndvi or pd.isna(y0_ndvi) or not post_ndvi:\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "    ndvi_baseline = np.mean(pre_ndvi)\n",
        "    ndvi_disturbance = ndvi_baseline - y0_ndvi\n",
        "    if ndvi_disturbance <= 0:\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "    ndvi_ratio = (max(post_ndvi) - y0_ndvi) / ndvi_disturbance\n",
        "\n",
        "    sight_ratio = np.nan\n",
        "    if key in share_piv.index:\n",
        "        srow = share_piv.loc[key]\n",
        "        pre_share = [v for v in (srow.get(y) for y in pre_years) if pd.notna(v)]\n",
        "        y0_share = srow.get(year)\n",
        "        post_share = [v for v in (srow.get(y) for y in recovery_post_years) if pd.notna(v)]\n",
        "        if pre_share and pd.notna(y0_share) and post_share:\n",
        "            share_baseline = np.mean(pre_share) + SMOOTH\n",
        "            y0_share_s = y0_share + SMOOTH\n",
        "            share_disturbance = share_baseline - y0_share_s\n",
        "            if share_disturbance > 0:\n",
        "                sight_ratio = (max(post_share) + SMOOTH - y0_share_s) / share_disturbance\n",
        "\n",
        "    post_heat = [v for v in (heat_row.get(y) for y in heat_post_years) if pd.notna(v)]\n",
        "    if not post_heat:\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "    heat_post_mean = np.mean(post_heat)\n",
        "    heat_anomaly = heat_post_mean - heat_baseline_mean.get(key, np.nan)\n",
        "\n",
        "    records.append({\n",
        "        \"ADM1_NAME\": state, \"ADM2_NAME\": div, \"fire_year\": year,\n",
        "        \"max_area_ha\": r[\"max_area_ha\"], \"major_fires\": r[\"major_fires\"],\n",
        "        \"ndvi_recovery_ratio\": ndvi_ratio, \"sightings_recovery_ratio\": sight_ratio,\n",
        "        \"heat_anomaly_postfire\": heat_anomaly,\n",
        "        \"division_total_sightings\": total_sightings_per_div.get(key, 0),\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "events_all = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
        "# RRI can be zero/negative (best post-fire value never exceeds the fire-year value); can't log-transform those.\n",
        "events_all = events_all[events_all[\"ndvi_recovery_ratio\"] > 0].copy()\n",
        "events_all[\"log_ndvi_ratio\"] = np.log(events_all[\"ndvi_recovery_ratio\"])\n",
        "events_all[\"log_severity\"] = np.log(events_all[\"max_area_ha\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "HABITAT_MIN_SIGHTINGS = 200\n",
        "events = events_all[(events_all[\"division_total_sightings\"] >= HABITAT_MIN_SIGHTINGS)\n",
        "                     & events_all[\"sightings_recovery_ratio\"].notna()\n",
        "                     & (events_all[\"sightings_recovery_ratio\"] > 0)].copy()\n",
        "events[\"log_sight_ratio\"] = np.log(events[\"sightings_recovery_ratio\"])\n",
        "events[\"recovery_gap\"] = events[\"log_ndvi_ratio\"] - events[\"log_sight_ratio\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"{len(events_all)} major-fire events with a usable NDVI recovery ratio + heat exposure \"\n",
        "      f\"({events_all['ADM2_NAME'].nunique()} divisions, states: {sorted(events_all['ADM1_NAME'].unique())})\")\n",
        "print(f\"{len(events)} of those also have a valid sightings recovery ratio in a habitat division \"\n",
        "      f\"({events['ADM2_NAME'].nunique()} divisions, states: {sorted(events['ADM1_NAME'].unique())})\")"
      ],
      "id": "5f332280",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "`events_all` (NDVI-only) and `events` (the habitat/sightings-gated\n",
        "subset, used for every sightings-side and recovery-gap test below) are\n",
        "each built **once** here and reused unchanged through §6-§10.\n",
        "\n",
        "Note the states actually retained in `events` above: the `>= 200`\n",
        "total-sightings habitat filter is a biogeographic fact, not a bug --\n",
        "these six indicator species are essentially south-eastern-Australia\n",
        "forest species and are rarely recorded in WA/NT/TAS/SA regardless of\n",
        "fire or NDVI coverage there, so the sightings-side and recovery-gap\n",
        "tests in §9-§10 necessarily run on whichever state(s) currently clear\n",
        "that bar (see §10 Limitations).\n",
        "\n",
        "# Descriptive overview"
      ],
      "id": "a1834b6a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
